[[:db/retract 17592186070175 :answer-field/choices 17592186070176] [:db/retract 17592186070175 :answer-field/choices 17592186070177] [:db/retract 17592186070175 :answer-field/choices 17592186070178] [:db/retract 17592186070175 :answer-field/choices 17592186070179] [:db/retract 17592186070175 :answer-field/choices 17592186070180] [:db/retract 17592186070115 :answer-field/choices 17592186070116] [:db/retract 17592186070115 :answer-field/choices 17592186070117] [:db/retract 17592186070115 :answer-field/choices 17592186070118] [:db/retract 17592186070115 :answer-field/choices 17592186070119] [:db/retract 17592186070115 :answer-field/choices 17592186070120] [:db/retract 17592186071246 :answer-field/choices 17592186071248] [:db/retract 17592186071246 :answer-field/choices 17592186071249] [:db/retract 17592186071246 :answer-field/choices 17592186071250] [:db/retract 17592186071246 :answer-field/choices 17592186071251] [:db/retract 17592186071246 :answer-field/choices 17592186071247] [:db/retract 17592186071240 :answer-field/choices 17592186071241] [:db/retract 17592186071240 :answer-field/choices 17592186071242] [:db/retract 17592186071240 :answer-field/choices 17592186071243] [:db/retract 17592186071240 :answer-field/choices 17592186071244] [:db/retract 17592186071240 :answer-field/choices 17592186071245] {:db/id 17592186073745 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b9f18fac-7576-5250-96fc-957f32166255" "question-6dba95b8-77df-52c1-b86b-bcff843030e4" "question-6a86a1c0-6162-5d37-ac2b-51fa127af01b" "question-598f0d12-0057-595a-88df-823e76f024dc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073642 :question/problem "Solve the equation $2x^3 - 6x^2 + 4x= 0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $2x.$ We can factor out the $2x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 2x({x}^{2}-3x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $x^2-3x+2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x({x}^{2}-3x+2) & =0 \\\\ 2x(x-1)(x-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $x = 0,$ $x = 1,$ and $x = 2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073746 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2ace9a7c-7f26-5739-81ff-450b62fa7683" "question-3a08949f-c53d-51fb-8ad8-329357cd31bd" "question-589b942b-2afa-544c-b0d4-95c41762ad42" "question-ae27ee23-00a1-5698-9779-e950f4da30dd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073643 :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $x^3 - x^2 - x = 3x^2 + 4x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form $P_n(x)=0.$ To do this, we subtract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-x & =3{x}^{2}+4x \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-x & =4x \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-5x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $x.$ We can factor out the $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-5x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-4x-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $x^2 - 4x - 5$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x({x}^{2}-4x-5) & =0 \\\\ x(x+1)(x-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $x = 0,$ $x = -1,$ and $x = 5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073747 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a572c317-dda1-5da3-ae6b-b774d6ba6280" "question-af7e750a-c93b-50d4-aa96-76ae41484ef4" "question-d93d4254-999a-5b0a-8dfe-92904ca8400e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073644 :question/problem "If $3x^5 + x^3 = 3x^3 - 5x^4,$ then what are the values of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form $P_n(x)=0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{5}+{x}^{3} & =3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{4} \\\\ 3{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}+{x}^{3} & =3{x}^{3} \\\\ 3{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $x^3.$ We can factor out the $x^3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+5x-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $3x^2+5x-2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+5x-2) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}(3x-1)(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $x = 0,$ $x = \\dfrac{1}{3},$ and $x = -2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-b9f18fac-7576-5250-96fc-957f32166255" :question/id #uuid "b9f18fac-7576-5250-96fc-957f32166255" :question/math-academy-id "q-71776" :question/problem "Solve the equation $2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+24x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $2x.$ We can factor out the $2x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+24x & =0 \\\\ 2x({x}^{2}+7x+12) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression ${x}^{2}+7x+12$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x({x}^{2}+7x+12) & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+4)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=-4,$ and $x=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-48adc87a-6d3d-5e14-b95f-10e72dbfc197"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-48adc87a-6d3d-5e14-b95f-10e72dbfc197" :answer-field/id #uuid "48adc87a-6d3d-5e14-b95f-10e72dbfc197" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cacccae7-e7f1-56e9-83c1-6a751d25d21d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ed80c47-53d9-5894-8530-36afb2d9d35c" "answer-cacccae7-e7f1-56e9-83c1-6a751d25d21d" "answer-55ce39c3-a5c4-556f-8a9d-09a127539449" "answer-76c51cb6-b218-5331-a5d1-7802a6ee2866" "answer-c8446242-0fc8-5e64-a859-345d430616a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ed80c47-53d9-5894-8530-36afb2d9d35c" :answer/id #uuid "2ed80c47-53d9-5894-8530-36afb2d9d35c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3,\\,0,\\,8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cacccae7-e7f1-56e9-83c1-6a751d25d21d" :answer/id #uuid "cacccae7-e7f1-56e9-83c1-6a751d25d21d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4,\\,-3,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55ce39c3-a5c4-556f-8a9d-09a127539449" :answer/id #uuid "55ce39c3-a5c4-556f-8a9d-09a127539449" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4,\\,0,\\,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76c51cb6-b218-5331-a5d1-7802a6ee2866" :answer/id #uuid "76c51cb6-b218-5331-a5d1-7802a6ee2866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4,\\,0,\\,6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8446242-0fc8-5e64-a859-345d430616a3" :answer/id #uuid "c8446242-0fc8-5e64-a859-345d430616a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,\\,3,\\,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6dba95b8-77df-52c1-b86b-bcff843030e4" :question/id #uuid "6dba95b8-77df-52c1-b86b-bcff843030e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-70388" :question/problem "Find the roots of the polynomial $p(y)=10{y}^{3}+5{y}^{2}-5y.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the roots of the polynomial, we must solve the equation $p(y)=0,$ that is\n\n$$\n10{y}^{3}+5{y}^{2}-5y=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $5y.$ We can factor out the $5y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y(2{y}^{2}+y-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $2{y}^{2}+y-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y(2{y}^{2}+y-1) & =0 \\\\ 5y(2y-1)(y+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $y=0,$ $y=\\frac{1}{2},$ and $y=-1$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d775bf5a-0368-53ae-878e-5cd650356f18"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d775bf5a-0368-53ae-878e-5cd650356f18" :answer-field/id #uuid "d775bf5a-0368-53ae-878e-5cd650356f18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2b89dd01-b3fc-5526-9c13-3a06aab8a233" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c084c6aa-2fc6-5f4f-b3a8-d6744f77733c" "answer-2b89dd01-b3fc-5526-9c13-3a06aab8a233" "answer-29b0aa04-be1e-54a7-b230-b4434a74a514" "answer-6a9dfe8f-8341-5528-919c-63a6c5c4a648" "answer-9972ffb9-d058-59a6-9b51-c552ecb84de2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c084c6aa-2fc6-5f4f-b3a8-d6744f77733c" :answer/id #uuid "c084c6aa-2fc6-5f4f-b3a8-d6744f77733c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1,\\,0,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b89dd01-b3fc-5526-9c13-3a06aab8a233" :answer/id #uuid "2b89dd01-b3fc-5526-9c13-3a06aab8a233" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29b0aa04-be1e-54a7-b230-b4434a74a514" :answer/id #uuid "29b0aa04-be1e-54a7-b230-b4434a74a514" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2,\\,0,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a9dfe8f-8341-5528-919c-63a6c5c4a648" :answer/id #uuid "6a9dfe8f-8341-5528-919c-63a6c5c4a648" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9972ffb9-d058-59a6-9b51-c552ecb84de2" :answer/id #uuid "9972ffb9-d058-59a6-9b51-c552ecb84de2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6a86a1c0-6162-5d37-ac2b-51fa127af01b" :question/id #uuid "6a86a1c0-6162-5d37-ac2b-51fa127af01b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70389" :question/problem "Solve for $t$ if $4{t}^{3}-20{t}^{2}+24t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $4t.$ We can factor out the $4t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{t}^{3}-20{t}^{2}+24t & =0 \\\\ 4t({t}^{2}-5t+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression ${t}^{2}-5t+6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4t({t}^{2}-5t+6) & =0 \\\\ 4t(t-2)(t-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $t=0$, $t=2$ and $t=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-014820dd-53d9-5997-9a0b-dbb6f0ddd6df"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-014820dd-53d9-5997-9a0b-dbb6f0ddd6df" :answer-field/id #uuid "014820dd-53d9-5997-9a0b-dbb6f0ddd6df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2d803a67-e01a-5dae-a6e3-d71ed0191880" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d11d3833-f957-59c7-a006-29a06f0b643a" "answer-6c74bc5f-77fa-5808-8bfd-22468b03eb0e" "answer-37e96be1-0228-5e41-a422-f5ac375955a0" "answer-a9ea1023-9d04-542b-8780-58eb7dba28c6" "answer-2d803a67-e01a-5dae-a6e3-d71ed0191880"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d11d3833-f957-59c7-a006-29a06f0b643a" :answer/id #uuid "d11d3833-f957-59c7-a006-29a06f0b643a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-2,\\,0,\\,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c74bc5f-77fa-5808-8bfd-22468b03eb0e" :answer/id #uuid "6c74bc5f-77fa-5808-8bfd-22468b03eb0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-5,\\,-2,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37e96be1-0228-5e41-a422-f5ac375955a0" :answer/id #uuid "37e96be1-0228-5e41-a422-f5ac375955a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-6,\\,-1,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9ea1023-9d04-542b-8780-58eb7dba28c6" :answer/id #uuid "a9ea1023-9d04-542b-8780-58eb7dba28c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,\\,1,\\,6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d803a67-e01a-5dae-a6e3-d71ed0191880" :answer/id #uuid "2d803a67-e01a-5dae-a6e3-d71ed0191880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,\\,2,\\,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074015 :question/problem "Solve the equation $6{z}^{3}-21{z}^{2}-90z=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $3z.$ We can factor out the $3z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{z}^{3}-21{z}^{2}-90z & =0 \\\\ 3z(2{z}^{2}-7z-30) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $2{z}^{2}-7z-30$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z(2{z}^{2}-7z-30) & =0 \\\\ 3z(2z+5)(z-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $z=0,$ $z=-\\frac{5}{2},$ and $z=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186070175 :answer-field/correct "answer-e4d9cfdf-e3f3-5aa1-80a4-8f44ea2ba2c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5059480d-49b5-5e4a-bd13-82ce2b77ee01" "answer-5713fbbf-27f4-5c95-b6fd-bfb010b612f8" "answer-6b8251d7-0c1c-57d3-82c1-96e020e790ba" "answer-e4d9cfdf-e3f3-5aa1-80a4-8f44ea2ba2c7" "answer-7033358f-af7b-5515-ab10-9200cdcc75f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5059480d-49b5-5e4a-bd13-82ce2b77ee01" :answer/id #uuid "5059480d-49b5-5e4a-bd13-82ce2b77ee01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-6,\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5713fbbf-27f4-5c95-b6fd-bfb010b612f8" :answer/id #uuid "5713fbbf-27f4-5c95-b6fd-bfb010b612f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b8251d7-0c1c-57d3-82c1-96e020e790ba" :answer/id #uuid "6b8251d7-0c1c-57d3-82c1-96e020e790ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{5}{2},\\,0,\\,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4d9cfdf-e3f3-5aa1-80a4-8f44ea2ba2c7" :answer/id #uuid "e4d9cfdf-e3f3-5aa1-80a4-8f44ea2ba2c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{5}{2},\\,0,\\,6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7033358f-af7b-5515-ab10-9200cdcc75f2" :answer/id #uuid "7033358f-af7b-5515-ab10-9200cdcc75f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=0,\\,5,\\,6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-598f0d12-0057-595a-88df-823e76f024dc" :question/id #uuid "598f0d12-0057-595a-88df-823e76f024dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-114097" :question/problem "Find the roots of the polynomial $p(w)=8{w}^{3}-20{w}^{2}-12w.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the roots of the polynomial, we must solve the equation $p(w)=0,$ that is\n\n$$\n8{w}^{3}-20{w}^{2}-12w=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $4w.$ We can factor out the $4w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4w(2{w}^{2}-5w-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $2{w}^{2}-5w-3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4w(2{w}^{2}-5w-3) & =0 \\\\ 4w(2w+1)(w-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $w=0,$ $w=-\\frac{1}{2},$ and $w=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0959ab45-d3bb-507d-9b03-97c7b3eb10dc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0959ab45-d3bb-507d-9b03-97c7b3eb10dc" :answer-field/id #uuid "0959ab45-d3bb-507d-9b03-97c7b3eb10dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-14dc1c65-04df-5fbd-be61-4477e30ea100" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2c17f057-bfa1-5976-b130-cd6d0a8fb8f9" "answer-14dc1c65-04df-5fbd-be61-4477e30ea100" "answer-f0adf3bb-6907-5333-bed7-5a181b9295d9" "answer-9d08a714-6f3f-5167-98b9-80593532b035" "answer-21aebf18-ce11-5430-a764-9bb724cacfd6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c17f057-bfa1-5976-b130-cd6d0a8fb8f9" :answer/id #uuid "2c17f057-bfa1-5976-b130-cd6d0a8fb8f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=-2,0,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14dc1c65-04df-5fbd-be61-4477e30ea100" :answer/id #uuid "14dc1c65-04df-5fbd-be61-4477e30ea100" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=-\\frac{1}{2},0,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0adf3bb-6907-5333-bed7-5a181b9295d9" :answer/id #uuid "f0adf3bb-6907-5333-bed7-5a181b9295d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=-\\frac{1}{2},1,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d08a714-6f3f-5167-98b9-80593532b035" :answer/id #uuid "9d08a714-6f3f-5167-98b9-80593532b035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=-\\frac{3}{2},0,6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21aebf18-ce11-5430-a764-9bb724cacfd6" :answer/id #uuid "21aebf18-ce11-5430-a764-9bb724cacfd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=0,2,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074005 :question/problem "Solve for $z$ where $-6{z}^{3}-12{z}^{2}+20z=3{z}^{2}-16z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(z)=0.$ To do this, we subtract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{z}^{3}-12{z}^{2}+20z & =3{z}^{2}-16z \\\\ -6{z}^{3}-15{z}^{2}+20z & =-16z \\\\ -6{z}^{3}-15{z}^{2}+36z & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $-3z.$ We can factor out the $-3z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{z}^{3}-15{z}^{2}+36z & =0 \\\\ -3z(2{z}^{2}+5z-12) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $2{z}^{2}+5z-12$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3z(2{z}^{2}+5z-12) & =0 \\\\ -3z(2z-3)(z+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $z=0,$ $z=\\frac{3}{2},$ and $z=-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186070115 :answer-field/correct "answer-af85b59e-19c9-5c0f-890e-e229261732cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2706b10-456e-5cf0-af26-738518efe438" "answer-01025723-2564-5015-9d6f-9159e6f39f1f" "answer-af85b59e-19c9-5c0f-890e-e229261732cc" "answer-03d8b461-4ae9-52a8-aca8-51e298ef0397" "answer-c0b19f27-5dfc-57bb-b7ed-81e28ee0fafb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2706b10-456e-5cf0-af26-738518efe438" :answer/id #uuid "b2706b10-456e-5cf0-af26-738518efe438" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01025723-2564-5015-9d6f-9159e6f39f1f" :answer/id #uuid "01025723-2564-5015-9d6f-9159e6f39f1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-3,\\,0,\\,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af85b59e-19c9-5c0f-890e-e229261732cc" :answer/id #uuid "af85b59e-19c9-5c0f-890e-e229261732cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-4,\\,0,\\,\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03d8b461-4ae9-52a8-aca8-51e298ef0397" :answer/id #uuid "03d8b461-4ae9-52a8-aca8-51e298ef0397" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{1}{3},\\,0,\\,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0b19f27-5dfc-57bb-b7ed-81e28ee0fafb" :answer/id #uuid "c0b19f27-5dfc-57bb-b7ed-81e28ee0fafb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=0,\\,4,\\,\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2ace9a7c-7f26-5739-81ff-450b62fa7683" :question/id #uuid "2ace9a7c-7f26-5739-81ff-450b62fa7683" :question/math-academy-id "q-3985" :question/problem "Solve for $t$ where $-2{t}^{3}-10{t}^{2}+10t=-14t-2{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(t)=0.$ To do this, we subtract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{t}^{3}-10{t}^{2}+10t & =-14t-2{t}^{2} \\\\ -2{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}+10t & =-14t \\\\ -2{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}+24t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $-2t.$ We can factor out the $-2t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}+24t & =0 \\\\ -2t({t}^{2}+4t-12) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression ${t}^{2}+4t-12$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2t({t}^{2}+4t-12) & =0 \\\\ -2t(t+6)(t-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $t=0,$ $t=-6,$ and $t=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7985aead-1b21-56ef-98f3-fd4a253086a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7985aead-1b21-56ef-98f3-fd4a253086a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "7985aead-1b21-56ef-98f3-fd4a253086a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5a5e4519-cc30-5396-bd1c-9cef58c7772d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e20eba27-efe7-579a-9a7f-eae6ba53a1ca" "answer-e7fb26bd-7ed2-5f2d-94d8-58300ffb1318" "answer-5a5e4519-cc30-5396-bd1c-9cef58c7772d" "answer-84a02a9d-8984-54df-8d54-f34ac7891575" "answer-0a49e338-c372-5407-9df4-fad1f40d4c65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e20eba27-efe7-579a-9a7f-eae6ba53a1ca" :answer/id #uuid "e20eba27-efe7-579a-9a7f-eae6ba53a1ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-1,\\,0,\\,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7fb26bd-7ed2-5f2d-94d8-58300ffb1318" :answer/id #uuid "e7fb26bd-7ed2-5f2d-94d8-58300ffb1318" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-3,\\,-1,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a5e4519-cc30-5396-bd1c-9cef58c7772d" :answer/id #uuid "5a5e4519-cc30-5396-bd1c-9cef58c7772d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-6,\\,0,\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84a02a9d-8984-54df-8d54-f34ac7891575" :answer/id #uuid "84a02a9d-8984-54df-8d54-f34ac7891575" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,\\,1,\\,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a49e338-c372-5407-9df4-fad1f40d4c65" :answer/id #uuid "0a49e338-c372-5407-9df4-fad1f40d4c65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,\\,2,\\,6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3a08949f-c53d-51fb-8ad8-329357cd31bd" :question/id #uuid "3a08949f-c53d-51fb-8ad8-329357cd31bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-37615" :question/problem "Find the solutions of the equation $20{p}^{3}+7{p}^{2}=6p.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(p)=0.$ To do this, we subtract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{p}^{3}+7{p}^{2} & =6p \\\\ 20{p}^{3}+7{p}^{2}-6p & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $p.$ We can factor out the $p$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{p}^{3}+7{p}^{2}-6p & =0 \\\\ p(20{p}^{2}+7p-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $20{p}^{2}+7p-6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(20{p}^{2}+7p-6) & =0 \\\\ p(5p-2)(4p+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $p=0,$ $p=\\frac{2}{5},$ and $p=-\\frac{3}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4f973cd9-bf32-5279-9138-1e6ff7e9e31b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f973cd9-bf32-5279-9138-1e6ff7e9e31b" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f973cd9-bf32-5279-9138-1e6ff7e9e31b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f921ee8e-f8e9-543a-8997-432bf272edf5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f4654cf-8099-5359-8263-b4873cfd74d9" "answer-f921ee8e-f8e9-543a-8997-432bf272edf5" "answer-95cea456-477e-5349-9e24-76b0bd2aaa7e" "answer-73b48f90-577a-5549-956b-b9cfd6428ccf" "answer-303a6c40-7dd3-5a1f-9ac2-fe9037107dec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f4654cf-8099-5359-8263-b4873cfd74d9" :answer/id #uuid "9f4654cf-8099-5359-8263-b4873cfd74d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-\\frac{2}{5},\\,0,\\,\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f921ee8e-f8e9-543a-8997-432bf272edf5" :answer/id #uuid "f921ee8e-f8e9-543a-8997-432bf272edf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-\\frac{3}{4},\\,0,\\,\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95cea456-477e-5349-9e24-76b0bd2aaa7e" :answer/id #uuid "95cea456-477e-5349-9e24-76b0bd2aaa7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-\\frac{4}{3},\\,0,\\,\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73b48f90-577a-5549-956b-b9cfd6428ccf" :answer/id #uuid "73b48f90-577a-5549-956b-b9cfd6428ccf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-\\frac{5}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-303a6c40-7dd3-5a1f-9ac2-fe9037107dec" :answer/id #uuid "303a6c40-7dd3-5a1f-9ac2-fe9037107dec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=0,\\,\\frac{2}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-589b942b-2afa-544c-b0d4-95c41762ad42" :question/id #uuid "589b942b-2afa-544c-b0d4-95c41762ad42" :question/math-academy-id "q-3981" :question/problem "If $15{r}^{3}-50{r}^{2}=-40r$, then $r=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(r)=0.$ To do this, we subtract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{r}^{3}-50{r}^{2} & =-40r \\\\ 15{r}^{3}-50{r}^{2}+40r & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $5r.$ We can factor out the $5r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{r}^{3}-50{r}^{2}+40r & =0 \\\\ 5r(3{r}^{2}-10r+8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $3{r}^{2}-10r+8$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5r(3{r}^{2}-10r+8) & =0 \\\\ 5r(3r-4)(r-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $r=0,$ $r=\\frac{4}{3},$ and $r=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1082cb6a-95fd-59f2-ab50-826ca5cf3578"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1082cb6a-95fd-59f2-ab50-826ca5cf3578" :answer-field/id #uuid "1082cb6a-95fd-59f2-ab50-826ca5cf3578" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-761b3c80-100a-5ec0-b40d-e37f484f6891" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9d57cb1-306c-5ebe-be17-8d75522b2940" "answer-ac1809a8-20e2-5b39-991b-3a166e873fba" "answer-a18ce679-6e85-500b-b3c5-b21e7df06b8e" "answer-0346dd7f-1ea8-565f-ae3a-2489bdd2b183" "answer-761b3c80-100a-5ec0-b40d-e37f484f6891"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9d57cb1-306c-5ebe-be17-8d75522b2940" :answer/id #uuid "d9d57cb1-306c-5ebe-be17-8d75522b2940" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=-2,\\,0,\\,\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac1809a8-20e2-5b39-991b-3a166e873fba" :answer/id #uuid "ac1809a8-20e2-5b39-991b-3a166e873fba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=-4,\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a18ce679-6e85-500b-b3c5-b21e7df06b8e" :answer/id #uuid "a18ce679-6e85-500b-b3c5-b21e7df06b8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=-\\frac{4}{3},\\,0,\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0346dd7f-1ea8-565f-ae3a-2489bdd2b183" :answer/id #uuid "0346dd7f-1ea8-565f-ae3a-2489bdd2b183" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=0,\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-761b3c80-100a-5ec0-b40d-e37f484f6891" :answer/id #uuid "761b3c80-100a-5ec0-b40d-e37f484f6891" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=0,\\,\\frac{4}{3},\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae27ee23-00a1-5698-9779-e950f4da30dd" :question/id #uuid "ae27ee23-00a1-5698-9779-e950f4da30dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-14007" :question/problem "Determine the real roots of the cubic equation $12{s}^{3}+12{s}^{2}-20s=6{s}^{2}+16s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(s)=0.$ To do this, we subtract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{s}^{3}+12{s}^{2}-20s & =6{s}^{2}+16s \\\\ 12{s}^{3}+6{s}^{2}-20s & =16s \\\\ 12{s}^{3}+6{s}^{2}-36s & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $6s.$ We can factor out the $6s$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{s}^{3}+6{s}^{2}-36s & =0 \\\\ 6s(2{s}^{2}+s-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $2{s}^{2}+s-6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6s(2{s}^{2}+s-6) & =0 \\\\ 6s(2s-3)(s+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $s=0,$ $s=\\frac{3}{2},$ and $s=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-971c6c2e-9221-5a95-aafb-62f84bc18983"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-971c6c2e-9221-5a95-aafb-62f84bc18983" :answer-field/id #uuid "971c6c2e-9221-5a95-aafb-62f84bc18983" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e63d264-ea50-58ed-916c-7de30c6c0798" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4582def6-f856-5add-b613-0218c9f9fe54" "answer-c08f4492-345f-5b87-8634-052cc34abc16" "answer-4e63d264-ea50-58ed-916c-7de30c6c0798" "answer-dc40935f-e545-5418-9a22-e109cc113b4c" "answer-f911e318-36c7-56ee-b300-a669a11ca6c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4582def6-f856-5add-b613-0218c9f9fe54" :answer/id #uuid "4582def6-f856-5add-b613-0218c9f9fe54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s=-2,\\,0,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c08f4492-345f-5b87-8634-052cc34abc16" :answer/id #uuid "c08f4492-345f-5b87-8634-052cc34abc16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s=-2,\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e63d264-ea50-58ed-916c-7de30c6c0798" :answer/id #uuid "4e63d264-ea50-58ed-916c-7de30c6c0798" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s=-2,\\,0,\\,\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc40935f-e545-5418-9a22-e109cc113b4c" :answer/id #uuid "dc40935f-e545-5418-9a22-e109cc113b4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s=-\\frac{3}{2},\\,0,\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f911e318-36c7-56ee-b300-a669a11ca6c1" :answer/id #uuid "f911e318-36c7-56ee-b300-a669a11ca6c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s=0,\\,2,\\,\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a572c317-dda1-5da3-ae6b-b774d6ba6280" :question/id #uuid "a572c317-dda1-5da3-ae6b-b774d6ba6280" :question/math-academy-id "q-114108" :question/problem "If $14{p}^{4}-10{p}^{3}+5{p}^{2}=2{p}^{4}+17{p}^{2},$ then what are the values of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14{p}^{4}-10{p}^{3}+5{p}^{2} & =2{p}^{4}+17{p}^{2} \\\\ 12{p}^{4}-10{p}^{3}+5{p}^{2} & =17{p}^{2} \\\\ 12{p}^{4}-10{p}^{3}-12{p}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $2{p}^{2}.$ We can factor out the $2{p}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{p}^{4}-10{p}^{3}-12{p}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{p}^{2}(6{p}^{2}-5p-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $6{p}^{2}-5p-6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{p}^{2}(6{p}^{2}-5p-6) & =0 \\\\ 2{p}^{2}(3p+2)(2p-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $p=0,$ $p=-\\frac{2}{3},$ and $p=\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7db8c159-2034-5a4d-9ed7-a18d7e127cc6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7db8c159-2034-5a4d-9ed7-a18d7e127cc6" :answer-field/id #uuid "7db8c159-2034-5a4d-9ed7-a18d7e127cc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1b6656eb-e900-52d1-80d6-743f4beaedf4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56d3c364-0918-5bee-aefe-a198ca16efe1" "answer-08e2c11b-95eb-5f08-a9a0-8be6291b080e" "answer-1b6656eb-e900-52d1-80d6-743f4beaedf4" "answer-8f183aaa-0947-5d53-96df-c8c4236d1225" "answer-17dca348-b860-5d6a-8c49-01c5dabaa699"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56d3c364-0918-5bee-aefe-a198ca16efe1" :answer/id #uuid "56d3c364-0918-5bee-aefe-a198ca16efe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-3,-\\frac{2}{3},0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08e2c11b-95eb-5f08-a9a0-8be6291b080e" :answer/id #uuid "08e2c11b-95eb-5f08-a9a0-8be6291b080e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-3,0,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b6656eb-e900-52d1-80d6-743f4beaedf4" :answer/id #uuid "1b6656eb-e900-52d1-80d6-743f4beaedf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-\\frac{2}{3},0,\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f183aaa-0947-5d53-96df-c8c4236d1225" :answer/id #uuid "8f183aaa-0947-5d53-96df-c8c4236d1225" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-\\frac{3}{2},0,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17dca348-b860-5d6a-8c49-01c5dabaa699" :answer/id #uuid "17dca348-b860-5d6a-8c49-01c5dabaa699" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=0,2,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-af7e750a-c93b-50d4-aa96-76ae41484ef4" :question/id #uuid "af7e750a-c93b-50d4-aa96-76ae41484ef4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114116" :question/problem "Find the roots of the polynomial $p(w)=60{w}^{6}-105{w}^{5}+45{w}^{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the roots of the polynomial, we must solve the equation $p(w)=0,$ that is\n\n$$\n60{w}^{6}-105{w}^{5}+45{w}^{4}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $15{w}^{4}.$ We can factor out the $15{w}^{4}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{w}^{4}(4{w}^{2}-7w+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $4{w}^{2}-7w+3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{w}^{4}(4{w}^{2}-7w+3) & =0 \\\\ 15{w}^{4}(4w-3)(w-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $w=0,$ $w=\\frac{3}{4},$ and $w=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d1caed9b-00a5-576f-9db3-b95772341ed6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d1caed9b-00a5-576f-9db3-b95772341ed6" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1caed9b-00a5-576f-9db3-b95772341ed6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f01b3681-4519-57fb-bc76-853ded546956" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0b30b2b8-aa8f-5c31-b7e3-bc987c2700fb" "answer-09e9fedc-4d5e-5788-be94-10e0f727eb89" "answer-bb2e1eb1-9a53-5789-b781-a03ef2aeb0b9" "answer-f01b3681-4519-57fb-bc76-853ded546956" "answer-e6b64a4c-411a-532f-abeb-5237ce881e24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b30b2b8-aa8f-5c31-b7e3-bc987c2700fb" :answer/id #uuid "0b30b2b8-aa8f-5c31-b7e3-bc987c2700fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=-2,0,\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09e9fedc-4d5e-5788-be94-10e0f727eb89" :answer/id #uuid "09e9fedc-4d5e-5788-be94-10e0f727eb89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=-\\frac{3}{2},0,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb2e1eb1-9a53-5789-b781-a03ef2aeb0b9" :answer/id #uuid "bb2e1eb1-9a53-5789-b781-a03ef2aeb0b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=0,\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f01b3681-4519-57fb-bc76-853ded546956" :answer/id #uuid "f01b3681-4519-57fb-bc76-853ded546956" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=0,\\frac{3}{4},1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6b64a4c-411a-532f-abeb-5237ce881e24" :answer/id #uuid "e6b64a4c-411a-532f-abeb-5237ce881e24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=0,\\frac{5}{3},2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074168 :question/problem "If $5{q}^{5}-7{q}^{4}+10{q}^{3}-6q=-{q}^{5}+11{q}^{4}-2{q}^{3}-6q,$ then what are the values of $q?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(q)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{q}^{5}-7{q}^{4}+10{q}^{3}-6q & =-{q}^{5}+11{q}^{4}-2{q}^{3}-6q \\\\ 6{q}^{5}-18{q}^{4}+10{q}^{3}-6q & =-2{q}^{3}-6q \\\\ 6{q}^{5}-18{q}^{4}+12{q}^{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $6{q}^{3}.$ We can factor out the $6{q}^{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{q}^{5}-18{q}^{4}+12{q}^{3} & =0 \\\\ 6{q}^{3}({q}^{2}-3q+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression ${q}^{2}-3q+2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{q}^{3}({q}^{2}-3q+2) & =0 \\\\ 6{q}^{3}(q-1)(q-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $q=0,$ $q=1,$ and $q=2.$\n\nTherefore, using the zero product rule, we have that the solutions are $0,\\,1$ and $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186071246 :answer-field/correct "answer-4c02e4f8-b708-5865-be16-cdfc2761fcb3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bb39f4bb-01e2-5f62-a94b-0ec48c3cca9f" "answer-1b1433db-adc1-52e3-b005-6ae48814f3e5" "answer-af95cf1e-df56-56ac-995c-d2531f2040e2" "answer-4c02e4f8-b708-5865-be16-cdfc2761fcb3" "answer-a7c01589-5305-5536-b97c-c321ed32e67f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb39f4bb-01e2-5f62-a94b-0ec48c3cca9f" :answer/id #uuid "bb39f4bb-01e2-5f62-a94b-0ec48c3cca9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b1433db-adc1-52e3-b005-6ae48814f3e5" :answer/id #uuid "1b1433db-adc1-52e3-b005-6ae48814f3e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=-2,\\,-1,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af95cf1e-df56-56ac-995c-d2531f2040e2" :answer/id #uuid "af95cf1e-df56-56ac-995c-d2531f2040e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c02e4f8-b708-5865-be16-cdfc2761fcb3" :answer/id #uuid "4c02e4f8-b708-5865-be16-cdfc2761fcb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=0,\\,1,\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7c01589-5305-5536-b97c-c321ed32e67f" :answer/id #uuid "a7c01589-5305-5536-b97c-c321ed32e67f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=2,\\,4,\\,6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074167 :question/problem "Find the roots of the polynomial $p(x)=2{x}^{4}-7{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the roots of the polynomial, we must solve the equation $p(x)=0,$ that is\n\n$$\n2{x}^{4}-7{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of ${x}^{2}.$ We can factor out the ${x}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}(2{x}^{2}-7x-15) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $2{x}^{2}-7x-15$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}(2{x}^{2}-7x-15) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(2x+3)(x-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=-\\frac{3}{2},$ and $x=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186071240 :answer-field/correct "answer-39cefa24-96d5-5d54-83a4-f8e9b6c17839" :answer-field/choices ["answer-65136a7e-c90f-5366-85b3-d50d34248626" "answer-38b8f840-c042-5c1b-aae8-140a0d4c0a09" "answer-b5b0dcf6-1eae-5d92-92a7-6126d3337254" "answer-39cefa24-96d5-5d54-83a4-f8e9b6c17839" "answer-894c9af7-3295-5667-8592-8ab4dbc017fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65136a7e-c90f-5366-85b3-d50d34248626" :answer/id #uuid "65136a7e-c90f-5366-85b3-d50d34248626" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,\\,0,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38b8f840-c042-5c1b-aae8-140a0d4c0a09" :answer/id #uuid "38b8f840-c042-5c1b-aae8-140a0d4c0a09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,\\,-\\frac{3}{2},\\,0,\\,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5b0dcf6-1eae-5d92-92a7-6126d3337254" :answer/id #uuid "b5b0dcf6-1eae-5d92-92a7-6126d3337254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2}{3},\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39cefa24-96d5-5d54-83a4-f8e9b6c17839" :answer/id #uuid "39cefa24-96d5-5d54-83a4-f8e9b6c17839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{2},\\,0,\\,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-894c9af7-3295-5667-8592-8ab4dbc017fb" :answer/id #uuid "894c9af7-3295-5667-8592-8ab4dbc017fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,\\,\\frac{3}{2},\\,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d93d4254-999a-5b0a-8dfe-92904ca8400e" :question/id #uuid "d93d4254-999a-5b0a-8dfe-92904ca8400e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70467" :question/problem "Find the roots of the polynomial $p(z)=18{z}^{4}+3{z}^{3}-3{z}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the roots of the polynomial, we must solve the equation $p(z)=0,$ that is\n\n$$\n18{z}^{4}+3{z}^{3}-3{z}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $3{z}^{2}.$ We can factor out the $3{z}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{z}^{2}(6{z}^{2}+z-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $6{z}^{2}+z-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{z}^{2}(6{z}^{2}+z-1) & =0 \\\\ 3{z}^{2}(3z-1)(2z+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $z=0,$ $z=\\frac{1}{3},$ and $z=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ee49f43f-642d-52e4-92e0-629fb560b5c7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ee49f43f-642d-52e4-92e0-629fb560b5c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee49f43f-642d-52e4-92e0-629fb560b5c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5f13abfe-652c-5ae7-98ae-1daa422c3094" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f13abfe-652c-5ae7-98ae-1daa422c3094" "answer-33b8c262-de59-5b53-9770-39b84a4898a8" "answer-8a1e9a9b-eba2-52b1-bcc4-60d934c2e6a5" "answer-cea2e85c-f504-5caa-8597-6774360787af" "answer-2cca6df7-9375-5547-918c-7f576ca1fd47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f13abfe-652c-5ae7-98ae-1daa422c3094" :answer/id #uuid "5f13abfe-652c-5ae7-98ae-1daa422c3094" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33b8c262-de59-5b53-9770-39b84a4898a8" :answer/id #uuid "33b8c262-de59-5b53-9770-39b84a4898a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a1e9a9b-eba2-52b1-bcc4-60d934c2e6a5" :answer/id #uuid "8a1e9a9b-eba2-52b1-bcc4-60d934c2e6a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{1}{6},\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cea2e85c-f504-5caa-8597-6774360787af" :answer/id #uuid "cea2e85c-f504-5caa-8597-6774360787af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{3}{2},\\,0,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cca6df7-9375-5547-918c-7f576ca1fd47" :answer/id #uuid "2cca6df7-9375-5547-918c-7f576ca1fd47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=0,\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075006 :tutorial/content "A **polynomial equation** is an equation that can be written in the form\n\n$$\nP_n(x)=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $P_n(x)$  is a polynomial of degree $n.$\nA **cubic equation** is a polynomial equation of degree $n=3.$\n\nTo solve a polynomial equation with no constant term, we factor the polynomial part using the greatest common factor.\nOnce we've done that, we can apply the zero product rule to the resulting factors.\n\nFor instance, consider the cubic equation $x^3-x=0.$\n\nFirst, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $x.$ We can factor out the $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $x^2-1$ using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ x(x+1)(x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, we conclude that the solutions are ${\\color{red}x=0},$ ${\\color{blue}x = -1},$ and ${\\color{purple}x=1}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073918 :activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
